{
 "description": "Section edge types (SPEC-v1 \u00a78.3 rule 3 as ruled by [W0-43], [W0-49], [W0-51] and [W0-52]). An edge a body operation creates where faces of two operands meet is a line, circle or ellipse iff (a) its two faces are a pair of the rule-3 list, classified with the named tests (the plane\u2013cone test of [W0-51] included), and (b) the engine's own curve lies within tol of a conic of that type; otherwise it is `bspline`. Each case is a valid `aicad.ir/1` document and, per feature id, the expected `status` and `edge_types`: the counts of the listed edge types summed over the feature entry's bodies (after \u00a78.3); a listed 0 means none, types not listed are not compared. `rule` and `note` are informative. Shared by Forge (forge-ir tests/v1_conformance_amendments.rs, through forge-regen) and the oracle (W7b).",
